# SHIPPED — Verified Product Capabilities & Proven Path

File: openOODA/SHIPPED.oot
This is what we have proved on disk. NORTHSTAR is the vision. ROADMAP is the active execution plan. Residual is wanted, not built.

## 1. Ground Truth & Proof

  Proof: files under `ooda/`, plus `oodac check oodac/main.oo`,
  or emit-c / emit-llvm + gcc/clang + run. `std/src` is not that proof.

## 2. Proven Capabilities

### Compiler Floor
  - Pin: v0.201.0-beta. Live check of `oodac/main.oo`: OK. RAM-cold about 164s; disk-warm new-process about 0.02s (179 modules).
  - C emit through `chs_rt`, then `gcc`. That is the product path.
  - Official rebuild is `../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build`. The old `.sh` path is gone.
  - `ooda run` is check + emit C + gcc + exec (`fixtures/hello.oo`).
  - LLVM hello works on the current host (emit-llvm + clang + run). Result `match` prints `ok`. Two-module import prints `2`. Lock: `scripts/open30_llvm_lock_smoke.oo`.
  - LLVM self-host IR: `oodac --backend llvm emit-llvm oodac/main.oo` contains oodac symbols (`@main`, `@parse_cli_argv`). Import fntab maps `List[String]` to `%OoSList` (`fixtures/llvm_fntab_probe.oo`). Builtin `Result` calls emit as `%OoResS`; `clang -c` of that IR exits 0 on a side ELF (`scripts/open68_clangc_smoke.oo`). Side LLVM-linked oodac (`emit-mods` + `chs_rt.c`, no `llvm-link`) stamp-walks `fixtures/hello.oo` with a real `check_listing_fresh` (not `ret i32 1`) and prints `OK` on a valid `g_` listing; a changed hello does not print OK. Lock: `scripts/open68_stamp_smoke.oo`. C emit + gcc remains the product path. Full gcc-parity (every oodac command, C path retired) is residual. Prior link lock: `scripts/open68_link_smoke.oo`.
  - Clang link of full oodac as a gcc replacement is residual. Lock: `scripts/open68_llvm_lock.oo`.
  - Standalone x86_64: `oodac emit-x86 fixtures/open69_hello.oo` writes `_start` that prints Hello; `as`+`ld` runs it. Not emit-c. AArch64 is residual. Lock: `scripts/open69_x86_smoke.oo`.
  - SECRET sinks include `process_exec`. Fail fixture refuses the secret.

### Capability Model & Sandboxing
  - Process-local tokens. Landlock is a real Linux jail under `&SysCap` (`oo_landlock_restrict`). Empty allowlists fail closed. Proved `OK: LANDLOCK_JAIL` on this host.
  - POSIX `setrlimit` is product under `&SysCap` (AS / NOFILE / CPU). Zero quotas fail closed.
  - `spawn` / `wait` / `kill` are real. Child env is filtered (`OODA_`/`OO_` and `PATH`).
  - Hostile probes: `env_get` denies host keys; zero `FsWriteCap` exits; child drops `HOST_SECRET`; attenuate forged parent differs. Lock: `scripts/hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo`.
  - `process_exec` is a shell line and a secret sink.
  - `GpuCap` CPU/noop launch is product. `emit_ptx` writes real kernel PTX text (`add.s64`); device GPU dispatch is residual. Not CUDA, not a device launch.
  - Hierarchical HMAC attenuation, kernel object-cap seals, and measured isolate (hash of payload+token+domain) are product. Not SGX/TDX/SEV hardware enclaves. HMAC-SHA256 of a cap payload string is product.
  - Bump arenas (`arena_create`/`alloc`/`reset`) under AllocCap, `&ArenaCap` as its own token, and `actor_restart` under ThreadCap are product.

### Standard Library & Developer Tooling
  - Product `ooda/std` has 402 tracked `.oo`. Live `oodac check` 2026-08-17: 402 OK. Org `std/` is the separate `openOODA/std` repo. Inventory: `audit/library_status.oot` (siblings <= 256). This pass: typecheck fixes; HKDF combined RFC 5869 A.1 in org `crypto/hkdf.oo`.
  - vscode still talks to `vscode/server/ooda-lsp.js`. `ooda lsp` is a multi-message stdio loop. Hover and definition name the identifier under the cursor, not the first `fn`. Lock: `scripts/lsp_cursor_smoke.oo`.
  - `ooda check`, `build`, `run`, `test`, `dump`, `outline`, `reflect`, `fix`, `patch`, `lsp`, `context`, `digest`, `health`, `pkg`, and `add` are native `.oo` in `cli/main.oo`. There is no `scripts/ooda_product.sh`.
  - Ingest git allow-list refuses HTTP, git://, and userinfo lookalikes before clone. Lock: `cli/pm_extract_proof.oo` and `qa/pm_allow_spine.oo`.
  - `crypto_sha256_internal("hello")` matches the FIPS hex. HMAC-SHA256 length is 64. AES-128-ECB encrypts one block to hex (NIST C.1).
  - `oodac emit-wasm` writes a `\0asm` module with one code body per source `fn` and an `ooda-fns` custom section. `path_join` and `nfa_simulate("[ab]", …)` plus `dfa_compile` emit+gcc+run.
  - `ooda test` sets `OODA_TEST=1` and runs verify constructors plus `assert_eq!` / `assert!`. `ooda run` does not run verify blocks.
  - `ooda fix` applies `E_CAP`, `E_IMP` (missing import), `E_TC`, `E_PARSE` (missing `}`), and `E_MUST` (discarded Result → `is_err` wrap). Multi-pass, max eight. It asks yes/no before it writes, unless `--yes`. Writes go through `write_file` and need `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` (unset still denies). No TTY and no `--yes` refuses. Absolute paths and symlinks are refused. Lock: `scripts/emust_autofix_smoke.oo`.
  - `ooda patch` replaces one function body from a file (`--replace-fn` / `--with`) through `write_file`. Absolute paths, `..`, and symlinks are refused.
  - HITL is not product. The human loop is `ooda fix`.
  - Tree `oodac` emits the product CLI. `cli/host_run.oo` is 205 lines. JSON check lives in `cli/json_check.oo`.
  - Check refuses unused `Ok`/`Err`/`Some`, `let _ =` / `let _:`, discarded `expect_*`, discarded Result-returning calls such as `write_file`, and discarded user `Result` calls such as `boom();`.
  - Annotated `Option`/`Result` match with only `_` is non-exhaustive.
  - `Result[Void, String]` emits `OoResV`. `Ok(void)` is a real empty Ok. JSON errors carry line, col, and a nonempty source path.
  - Multi-file check reports per-file line/col (import lines kept as blanks).
  - `oodac check --json-errors` is in-process. No capture `.sh`. Product CLI also converts.
  - Named emit+gcc+run set: `scripts/ci_open_run.oo` (hello, int_main, open_ci_add).
  - Named emit-llvm+clang+run lock: `scripts/open30_llvm_lock_smoke.oo` (match `ok`, two-module `2`).
  - QA master is pure `.oo`. From `qa/`: `../ooda/bin/ooda run ./qa_master.oo` prints `qa_master: PASSED` (22 green). Top-level `qa/*.sh` runners are gone. Residual: broken fixtures in the `qa_master.oo` header and `e2e/*.sh`.
  - Two `emit-c` of `fixtures/hello.oo` are byte-identical. Named multi-backend lock: emit-c (hello/int_main/open_ci_add), emit-llvm, and emit-wasm are stable across two runs (`scripts/bit_identical_emit_lock.oo`). gcc binaries are not claimed bit-identical without strip+repro flags (OPEN-71).
  - `import_c` / header path and `lto_xlang_link` (gcc `-flto`) are product; emit may write `#include`. Not residual refuse.
  - Check-time SMT folds const `requires` / `ensures` / `spec` in fn headers. Full general symbolic SMT is residual.
  - `TraitDecl` and monomorphization are product.
  - `bare_metal_init` is product (hosted canary after zeroing a static page).
  - Official rebuild does not export `PURE_SKIP_CHECK`. That flag is opt-in only.
  - Proved 2026-08-15 on `./bin/ooda` and `./oodac/oodac` rebuilt from tree sources.
  - ROADMAP Residual names host-lint leftovers gone: no `ooda/fixtures/pm_launch_tamper.py`; `audit/library_status*.oot` each <= 256. Stay-residual facts (paused install, HITL, vscode `ooda-lsp.js`, `qa/e2e/*.sh`, AArch64, device GPU, SGX/TDX/SEV, full SMT) stay residual, not this-cycle `[ ]` work. Lock: `scripts/open51_hygiene_smoke.oo`. C emit + gcc remains the product path. ROADMAP Open holds honesty rows. Compiler leftovers and library leftovers stay on that list for other agents.

## 3. Residual (Wanted in NORTHSTAR / ROADMAP, Not Built)

  - Org `std/` volume certification is residual (named proves only; `audit/library_status.oot`).
  - Full gcc-parity LLVM oodac (every command, C path retired) is residual. Side linked hello stamp-walk is product.
  - AArch64 backend is residual (standalone x86_64 is product).
  - Device GPU dispatch is residual. PTX text emit is product; launching on a GPU is not.
  - SGX / TDX / SEV hardware enclaves are residual. Measured isolate is product.
  - Full SMT solver / general symbolic is residual. Const + header `requires` / `ensures` / `spec` fold is product.
  - Leftover list: `ROADMAP.oot` Open. Stale leftover words (old cold-check seconds and module counts, import_c refuse, empty-disk registry, AES-exits, clang-link-is-next) sit in the closed stale-word log, not as this-cycle leftover. Lock: `scripts/open52_stale_smoke.oo`. Honesty rows, compiler leftovers, and library leftovers sit under Open. C emit + gcc remains the product path.

